  "id": "cumulative-distribution-function",
  "term": "cumulative distribution function",
  "definition": "A cumulative distribution function is a way of describing how values are distributed in a population by showing, for any chosen value, how much of the population falls at or below it. In survey research, estimating this function helps researchers understand the distribution of a characteristic in a finite population, even when data come from complex sampling designs and some people do not respond.",
